{"id":"000VX4","title":"Check-In","author":"ChinStrap","solvedCount":3,"difficulty":4,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-06T18:08:02+00:00","posted":"Heute, 19:04 Uhr","rules":"Tried a different kind of Battenburg. Thanks to all testers and I hope you enjoy!\n\nPlay Now! →\n\nRules\n\nNormal Sudoku• Normal sudoku rules apply.\n\nNumbered Rooms• Every outside cell has a numbered rooms clue. Some have fallen off.\n• A clue gives the digit that must appear in the Nth position looking into the grid in that row/column, where N is the digit in the first position.\n• That Nth cell is the clue's target cell.\n\nActivated Cells• A cell is activated if it is the target cell of any numbered rooms clue.\n• A cell can be activated more than once (up to once for each of the four edges of the grid).\n• For example, row 2 column 3 is activated if there is a 2 in r1c3, a 3 in r2c1, an 8 in r9c3, or a 7 in r2c9.\n\nActivated Battenburg• A door mark at the corner of four cells means those four cells form a checkerboard of activated and non-activated cells, in some order.\n• All such 2x2s are marked, so no unmarked 2x2 is a checkerboard.","solutionCode":"Row 5, left to right (9 digits)","tags":["Sudoku"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/7rapu6k08g?setting-nogrid=true","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{"nogrid":"true"},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/7rapu6k08g?setting-nogrid=true","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":11,"cols":11,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-06T18:08:02+00:00"}